# lf icons. Two columns: a pattern, then one glyph.
#
# The glyphs are Nerd Font code points, which the shell, kitty and foot already
# require -- install.sh declares AdwaitaMono Nerd Font, so this file adds no
# dependency. On a machine whose font is not patched every one of these renders
# as a hollow box, which is the whole failure mode: annoying, never fatal.
#
# Deliberately small. This is the Font Awesome file-type family -- U+F07B and
# the U+F1C* block -- that every Nerd Font release has carried, rather than the
# larger per-language sets that move between releases and leave boxes behind on
# whichever machine upgraded last.
#
# A line with only a pattern and no glyph does not mean "no icon": lf reads it
# as "disable the rule for this type". Every line below has two columns.

